PROCEDURALLY GENERATED HIDING PLACES
====================================
diagonal_count_cohn_map: criteria=(4, 5, 5, 5, 3, 5) :: layer counts are base-N digits; prime profile integer certifies irreducibility
centered_magnetization_slice: criteria=(5, 5, 4, 5, 4, 4) :: coefficient magnitudes are layer-imbalance slices through tiling space
fiber_entropy_vs_irreducibility: criteria=(4, 4, 3, 5, 5, 4) :: same polynomial profile can hide many H-values and SCC shapes
root_argument_tournament: criteria=(5, 3, 4, 2, 3, 3) :: orient roots by argument/real part; reducible factors become conjugation-stable modules
newton_polygon_edge_tournament: criteria=(4, 4, 4, 3, 4, 4) :: vertices are Newton edges; orientations by slope/support dominance
finite_field_factor_race: criteria=(4, 5, 5, 2, 3, 4) :: orient primes by factorization type of f mod p and edge flips across p
evaluation_time_tournament: criteria=(3, 5, 4, 3, 3, 4) :: vertices are n-values; edge by which value gives stronger Singh certificate
derivative_trace_tournament: criteria=(4, 4, 4, 3, 4, 4) :: Singh derivative conditions become a hierarchy of trace/support gates
galois_orbit_recombination: criteria=(5, 2, 5, 2, 4, 2) :: subsets of roots oriented by stabilizer size and trace integrality
code_support_polynomial_lift: criteria=(4, 3, 3, 4, 5, 3) :: length-72 support moves become coefficient-layer tilings with fixed low terms
idea_tournament={'score_hist': {0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1, 6: 1, 7: 1, 8: 1, 9: 1}, 'directed_3cycles': 0, 'edge_flips_vs_novelty_only': 15, 'ranking': ['diagonal_count_cohn_map', 'centered_magnetization_slice', 'fiber_entropy_vs_irreducibility', 'newton_polygon_edge_tournament', 'finite_field_factor_race', 'derivative_trace_tournament', 'evaluation_time_tournament', 'root_argument_tournament', 'code_support_polynomial_lift', 'galois_orbit_recombination']}

ASSUMPTION CHALLENGE
====================
Considered vertex sets: arcs, coefficient layers, layer profiles,
fixed coefficient-magnitude slices, roots, factor subsets, finite primes,
evaluation times, Newton polygon edges, derivative obligations, code
support moves, and LRC denominator resources.
Chosen primary quotient: diagonal profiles of fixed-path tilings.
Preserved: the user's triangular coefficient-layer geometry, Cohn prime
certificates, sign/magnitude slices, and the fact that many tournaments can
share one coefficient profile.
Destroyed: individual arc arrangement, most H/SCC data, and actual
asymptotic Bunyakovsky information.  The fiber-H audit measures that loss.
